    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51a53670_a496c046",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-25T21:23:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "import_leaf() just sets unimported_leaf_data-\u003ehead to \u0026imported_leaf_data-\u003ehead. so, head-\u003epub_len comes from the original data. \n\niiuc, the only place we check pub_len is in validate_leaf_header, and the only check we have there is that if minor is one of the known versions then pub_len + sec_len \u003d\u003d expected_len. so, for unknown minors for the current major any pub_len is accepted. and even for known minors, pub_len can be \u003e sizeof(leaf_public_data_t) if sec_len is small? \n\nshall we additionally check imported_leaf_data-\u003ehead-\u003epub_len before doing memcpy with it here? or maybe this extra check already exists and I\u0027m missing it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac6b532a_4e3fbfe4",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T09:27:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right, we don\u0027t explicitly check that pub_len \u003c\u003d sizeof(leaf_public_data_t). An indirect check is done in hmac validation, where the header data is included in the hash.\n\nConsidering that we might want to keep the possibility of handling the leaves from the future, I think it\u0027s safer to go with min(pub_len, sizeof(leaf_public_data_t)) in memcpy and not apply an explicit check on pub_len.",
      "parentUuid": "51a53670_a496c046",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "543f9760_57edbc9e",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T14:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We intentionally left out a check to see if pub_len was equal to the struct size because we do want to be able to drop fields for rollback. In the case we create a new version that we don\u0027t want to allow rollbacks for, all that is needed is to increment the major version.",
      "parentUuid": "ac6b532a_4e3fbfe4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f0c221b_8dab8de3",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T18:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s all fine, but what happens if I current send a command with major\u003d0 (current), minor\u003d2 (\u003ecurrent) and some bogus length. Are we protected from that?",
      "parentUuid": "543f9760_57edbc9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b838359f_e18b469a",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T19:41:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do have checks to make sure the pub_length an sec_length match with the overall packet size reported in the header length field.\nThe HMAC has to be valid for the leaf to be accepted, so it would have to to be created by a valid version to be used.\n\nWe do need to make sure we don\u0027t run into a case were we have a pointer to the pub or sec section that isn\u0027t full length with fields that are accessed because accesses to that pointer might be invalid see:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/pinweaver.c?rcl\u003db83e555952336d583c19b26bfe026908ca70e196\u0026l\u003d95 \n\nThis happens:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/pinweaver.c?rcl\u003db83e555952336d583c19b26bfe026908ca70e196\u0026l\u003d467\n\nFor this reason we need to set a minimum value for pub_len that is at least big enough for the label.",
      "parentUuid": "3f0c221b_8dab8de3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2e84895_73e7dc1a",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T20:15:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok, so, to make sure I get it right: safe_memcmp(hmac, request-\u003eunimported_leaf_data.hmac, sizeof(hmac)) which is done right before calling decrypt_leaf_data() is what protects us from bad sizes. this way we know that whatever we have in imported_leaf_data structure was created an hmac-ed by cr50. and cr50 would never put a too long size in the structure. correct?\n\nif so, sounds good. I\u0027d still prefer that min(pub_len, sizeof(leaf_public_data_t)) or even \"if (pub_len \u003e sizeof(leaf_public_data_t)) return error;\" approach, just to protect from bugs in cr50 itself. but it indeed becomes optional.",
      "parentUuid": "b838359f_e18b469a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1de70c99_38ecbc88",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 292,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-29T08:53:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve set to use min of lengths. When we have a leaf from the future, it\u0027s possible that pub_len from head is bigger than the sizeof public_data. So, it\u0027s good to copy the minimum in that case, because the new fields should come at the end of public_data structure.",
      "parentUuid": "f2e84895_73e7dc1a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ddd520c_7dd4018c",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 479,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-25T21:23:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what should happen if major \u003d\u003d PW_LEAF_MAJOR_VERSION and minor \u003e PW_LEAF_MINOR_VERSION?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 479,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a866c0d5_e55dc4e1",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 479,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T09:27:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems like it was decided in the initial implementation to allow this use case, there\u0027s a test that checks it: https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/test/pinweaver.c?q\u003dpinweaver.c+file:%5Esrc/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026dr\u0026l\u003d2030\n\nI guess the intent is to be able to handle the rollback of CR50 code. Allen, do you have more information on this?",
      "parentUuid": "4ddd520c_7dd4018c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 479,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba13655d_93431a91",
        "filename": "common/pinweaver.c",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 479,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T14:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this case we want to allow a roll back that effectively loses the data in the extra fields. If we don\u0027t want that behavior, we can increment the major version.",
      "parentUuid": "a866c0d5_e55dc4e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 479,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 479,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9b9d860_0a13069f",
        "filename": "include/pinweaver_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-25T21:23:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so, remind me again: we decided to change that? \nwhat happens if we have this new version of cr50 running on the same device with old OS that uses PW_MAX_PATH_SIZE of 1536 and sends PW_INSERT_LEAF with protocol_version\u003d0 and h_aux height of 16? \n\nwhat happens to devices that are already using PINs and have already created trees with old height: iiuc, validate_request_with_path() \u003e validate_tree() \u003e validate_tree_parameters() will fail, so old PINs will stop working? or do I miss something?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0a810ea_b550b7af",
        "filename": "include/pinweaver_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1144419
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T09:27:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In current code we use the aux height \u003d 14 / 2 \u003d 7 (https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform2/cryptohome/le_credential_backend.h?type\u003dcs\u0026q\u003dkLengthLabels\u0026sq\u003dpackage:\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d17).\n\nAnd we don\u0027t change the height of the tree IIUC. When the tree is full, we just return that a new label cannot be created. So, I don\u0027t see how we could have a request with height \u003e 10.\n\nThis constant had to be decreased because the size of leaf_public_data_t has increased and the validation from here: https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/pinweaver.c?q\u003dPW_MAX_PATH_SIZE+file:%5Esrc/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026dr\u003dC\u0026l\u003d37\nwould fail.",
      "parentUuid": "d9b9d860_0a13069f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa67d0c1_b2037681",
        "filename": "include/pinweaver_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T14:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Igor is right about the logic behind our dropping the max path length like this. Had we allowed for tree resizing this would potentially break the case where the tree parameters led to packets that were too big. Those packets would be rejected.",
      "parentUuid": "a0a810ea_b550b7af",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ce61a7b_f6acb24e",
        "filename": "include/pinweaver_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160200
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T14:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So far we have only used a fixed height and fan out so it should be safe to make this change. The new messages wouldn\u0027t fit with the previous max path size, so this change is needed.",
      "parentUuid": "d9b9d860_0a13069f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "081476bb7561a64e15095c68d93f5637d15355b6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e652d37_194f8c6a",
        "filename": "include/pinweaver_types.h",
        "patchSetId": 37
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-26T18:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if the currently used tree height (and as the result, the h_aux.size()) is below the new reduced max, then no problem indeed - the existing devices with already established PINs will continue to work. \nif that was not the case, we\u0027d need some migration on the host side, I guess.",
      "parentUuid": "aa67d0c1_b2037681",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 29
      },
